The code, and the data we wrote ourselves, are released under the MIT License (see
LICENSE).

This repository also holds data compiled from, or pointing to, third-party sources.
Their owners keep their rights, and none of them endorses this project. Care facts from
gardening publishers are restated in our own words, with a link to the source page in
each row; no publisher's text is copied. `scripts/check_copied_text.py` checks this: it
fails if any data field shares 8 or more words in a row with a page that row cites.

