LIVE SERVICES

The app also asks these services at run time. Nothing they return is stored in this
repository.

Open-Meteo (https://open-meteo.com)
  Weather, the 2-week forecast, past weather (archive API) and place-name search
  (geocoding API). API data under CC BY 4.0: "Weather data by Open-Meteo.com". Open-Meteo
  combines national weather services' models, Copernicus/ECMWF reanalysis and the
  GeoNames place list (CC BY 4.0); the full list is at https://open-meteo.com/en/licence.
  The free API is for non-commercial use only. Anyone running a commercial copy needs
  an Open-Meteo API plan.

postcodes.io (https://postcodes.io)
  Turns a typed UK postcode into a rough location. Code MIT. Great Britain postcode data
  under the OS OpenData licence; Northern Ireland ("BT") postcodes under the ONSPD
  licence, free for non-commercial use only.
  Contains Ordnance Survey data (c) Crown copyright and database right.
  Contains Royal Mail data (c) Royal Mail copyright and database right.
  Contains National Statistics data (c) Crown copyright and database right.
  Contains NRS data (c) Crown copyright and database right.

OpenPlantBook (https://open.plantbook.io)
  Light, soil-moisture and temperature bands for a plant outside our own list (needs
  free API credentials). Used under OpenPlantBook's own terms of use; no data licence
  is stated, so none of its data is shipped here.

Royal Horticultural Society plant pages (https://www.rhs.org.uk)
  For a plant outside our list, the app reads that species' RHS page and uses its
  growing conditions for that one answer. Pages are cached only on the running server
  (data/pages/, never committed). RHS copyright; we link the page and do not copy its
  text.

Web search (Tavily, Exa, TinyFish)
  The follow-up chat can search trusted gardening sites. Each result keeps its
  publisher's copyright and is linked, not copied. Each service is used under its own
  terms.
